  "limitations": [
    "Observer, native QPC and Lua time have different origins. Only within-clock durations are compared here.",
    "Observer gaps are not exact load spans. Trial native spans are exact instrumented scopes, while baseline has no equivalent native trace.",
    "Mode1 often starts before the first captured sample. Aligning its first positive alpha removes the observed one-tick start offset; it is not the full request latency.",
    "Manager and transition fields are read non-atomically, so occasional count/alpha disagreement or missing alpha samples can reflect polling.",
    "Animation alpha is not necessarily clamped to1: TELEPORT mode4 legitimately exceeds1 in the native reference.",
    "One run per animation/rate proves this sampled matrix, not a repeatability distribution, every transition style, or pixel-level smoothness."
  ]
